<script>
import getDealSource from 'crm/src/deals/getDeal.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import DealTabs from 'crm/src/deals/lib/DealTabs.abide'
import dealTabsSource from 'crm/src/deals/lib/DealTabs.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import dealTabsTestSource from 'crm/src/deals/lib/DealTabs.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }

import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="Tabs switch between views of one record">
        <Example
            id="deal-tabs"
            title="`Tabs` — a tab per view, and one panel showing the selected one"
            summary="A deal's details, its value and its stage, one at a time. Click a tab, or focus one and move with the arrow keys."
            files={{
                'src/deals/lib/DealTabs.abide': dealTabsSource,
                'src/deals/getDeal.handler.ts': getDealSource,
                'src/deals/lib/DealTabs.test.ts': dealTabsTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <DealTabs />
        </Example>

        <p>Import it as <code>import Tabs from '@abide/abide/Tabs.abide'</code>. Hand it the
            tabs, the <code>key</code> each is told apart by, and bind <code>selected</code> to the
            key of the one showing. Its children are the panel. Read the selected key in them to
            choose what to show, as the card does.</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Prop</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>id</code></td><td>the root's id; each tab's id and the panel's are built from it</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>tabs</code></td><td>the tabs, in the order they render, as any items you like</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>key</code></td><td>what tells one tab from another, and what <code>selected</code> holds</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>label</code></td><td>a tab's text; its key where there is none</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>bind:selected</code></td><td>the selected tab's key, read and set; the first tab until one is picked</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Tab</code></td><td>an inline component rendering a tab's content, handed <code>item</code>, for an icon beside a name</td></tr>
                <tr><td>children</td><td>the panel's content</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Key, on a focused tab</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>ArrowRight · ArrowLeft</td><td>selects the next or the previous tab, round the ends</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Home · End</td><td>selects the first or the last tab</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>A key moves focus to the tab it selects. Only the selected tab is in the page's tab
            order, so Tab moves from it to the panel rather than through every tab. Switching
            writes the marks on two tabs and leaves the rest alone. The panel keeps its element,
            and what changes inside it is whatever your children read from the selected key.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Styling tabs by their parts and states">
        <p>The tabs ship no styles and write no class. Every element you can style carries a
            <code>data-part</code>, and the selected tab carries <code>data-selected</code>. Any
            attribute you pass, <code>class</code> included, lands on the root. The file tabs on
            every card of these docs are this component, styled from the docs' own stylesheet.</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Part</th><th>States</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>the root <code>div</code></td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
                <tr><td>the row of tabs</td><td><code>tablist</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
                <tr><td>each tab's <code>button</code></td><td><code>tab</code></td><td><code>data-selected</code> on the selected tab</td></tr>
                <tr><td>the panel</td><td><code>panel</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>You write</th><th>It styles</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>{'[data-part=tab][data-selected] { … }'}</code></td><td>the selected tab, from a stylesheet</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>{'class="[&_[data-selected]]:font-semibold"'}</code></td><td>the same, as a Tailwind utility on the root</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>{'class="[&_[data-part=tablist]]:flex"'}</code></td><td>the row of tabs, from the root</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>{'class="[&_[data-part=panel]]:p-4"'}</code></td><td>the panel, from the root</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
